course: dictionary
lesson: 2857
title: Doleful: sad and gloomy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Doleful means very sad and gloomy. A doleful face looks miserable, and a doleful voice sounds sad. «The Rat paid no heed to his doleful self-reproaches.» Self-reproaches means blaming yourself, so the Rat is feeling gloomy about his own mistakes.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Doleful news makes people sad, and a doleful song sounds slow and unhappy. Try the swap test: put sad in place of doleful. «Doleful news» becomes «sad news», which still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Writers use doleful to show a mood. In Alice in Wonderland the Mock Turtle sings in a doleful voice, and in The Wind in the Willows Toad is doleful in prison. Look at the words around doleful to see how the character feels.
fact: Doleful means very sad and gloomy.
fact: Doleful can describe a face, a voice, a sound or news.
fact: «Doleful news» means news that causes sadness.
fact: Sad is a useful swap for doleful, but doleful is stronger and more gloomy.
fact: Writers choose doleful to paint a feeling, so look for the mood in the words around it.
exercise: «The Mock Turtle sang in a doleful voice.» What does doleful mean here? | Hungry for food | Quick and jumpy | *Very sad and gloomy | Loud and cheerful
exercise: «The news was doleful, and the whole village went quiet.» What does doleful suggest? | Causing a long walk | Causing laughter | Causing a bright party | *Causing sadness
exercise: Which word is the best swap for doleful in «a doleful song»? | fast | *sad | loud | happy
test: «Toad looked doleful in his cell.» What does doleful show about Toad? | He is excited about his trip | *He is sad and miserable | He is very cold and wet | He is fast asleep
test: Which sentence uses doleful correctly? | The doleful dog ran and jumped in the park. | The doleful sun shone on the sandy beach. | *The doleful children sat by the window, missing their mum. | The doleful children danced and laughed at the party.
exam: «The Rat paid no heed to his doleful self-reproaches.» What does doleful mean in this sentence? | Hungry and tired | Brave and bold | Clean and bright | *Very sad and gloomy
